1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,687
HANDOFF Ledger makes a release handoff inspectable.

2
00:00:03,687 --> 00:00:09,580
This is an edited screenshot walkthrough of saved, verified local model executions.

3
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:12,526
SampleDock is our original fictional fixture.

4
00:00:12,526 --> 00:00:18,418
The screens and receipts come from the actual application, with waiting time

5
00:00:18,418 --> 00:00:18,910
abbreviated.

6
00:00:20,417 --> 00:00:23,358
A release announcement says every check passed.

7
00:00:23,358 --> 00:00:28,401
The records show three different decisions: blank display names are rejected, an

8
00:00:28,401 --> 00:00:33,863
upgrade loses the saved locale, and the Japanese language review has not run.

9
00:00:33,863 --> 00:00:39,326
This is synthetic evidence, designed to expose the difference between a failure and

10
00:00:39,326 --> 00:00:40,166
missing evidence.

11
00:00:44,417 --> 00:00:49,360
The running view is a captured moment, not continuous video.

12
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:51,337
Waiting time is abbreviated.

13
00:00:51,337 --> 00:00:54,798
OpenMinion collects evidence through three read-only tools.

14
00:00:54,798 --> 00:00:58,752
Its official schema interface then generates a report.

15
00:00:58,752 --> 00:01:03,201
Pydantic and independent evidence checks decide whether it succeeds.

16
00:01:04,708 --> 00:01:09,043
The model preserves all three states: supported, contradicted, and unknown.

17
00:01:09,043 --> 00:01:15,112
It writes concrete findings for the next owner: investigate locale loss and perform the

18
00:01:15,112 --> 00:01:16,412
missing Japanese review.

19
00:01:16,412 --> 00:01:22,481
The application does not fill in a successful fallback report when the model omits

20
00:01:22,481 --> 00:01:23,348
those findings.

21
00:01:28,708 --> 00:01:32,762
The migration citation leads to the exact failed check.

22
00:01:32,762 --> 00:01:38,166
Independent validation checks the source hash, the quoted excerpt, and the claim

23
00:01:38,166 --> 00:01:38,617
classification.

24
00:01:38,617 --> 00:01:44,471
A reviewer can inspect the evidence behind the conclusion, instead of treating a

25
00:01:44,471 --> 00:01:46,273
persuasive summary as proof.

26
00:01:50,708 --> 00:01:53,822
The captured run took 84.3 seconds.

27
00:01:53,822 --> 00:01:55,378
Five calls succeeded;

28
00:01:55,378 --> 00:01:57,973
a zero-index read was rejected.

29
00:01:57,973 --> 00:02:05,238
The coverage guard required a bounded second Agent turn, which read a valid span.

30
00:02:05,238 --> 00:02:07,313
Both validation layers passed.

31
00:02:07,313 --> 00:02:13,540
Earlier fresh sessions needed no recovery: six successful calls in fifty-five seconds,

32
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:15,616
then seven in fifty-three.

33
00:02:15,616 --> 00:02:19,248
These are fixture measurements, not general reliability.

34
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:25,039
An earlier valid JSON answer omitted unknowns and risks;

35
00:02:25,039 --> 00:02:26,945
our verifier rejected it.

36
00:02:26,945 --> 00:02:29,804
This prototype reads small structured files.

37
00:02:29,804 --> 00:02:34,569
It does not run project tests or approve a release.

38
00:02:34,569 --> 00:02:37,428
Its explanations still need human review.

39
00:02:37,428 --> 00:02:38,858
Codex assisted development.

40
00:02:38,858 --> 00:02:44,100
HANDOFF Ledger leaves the next owner a handoff they can inspect.

